The planning rows of the registry, read from the texts of registry files and held to the rules a schema cannot state: milestones, stretches, epochs, members, windows, landings and the rest, each a fact appended and naming the row it replaces. It depends on `kaski-tickets` for the one reading of a row, and the tickets crate names nothing of planning, so the tickets tool, its makers and the console build both and judge a write alike.
